{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 30, "timestamp": 1795081170, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/sh", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}}
[0.009109, "o", "\r\n# Author side of cheeseless. The agents below are scripted stand-ins, not LLMs.\r\n# The repo has a spec and a smoke test; there are no hidden tests yet.\r\n"]
[0.009236, "o", "$ git ls-files\r\nREADME.md\r\nacceptance/contract/criteria.yaml\r\nacceptance/contract/spec.md\r\nacceptance/contract/test_smoke.py\r\nsrc/toy/__init__.py\r\nsrc/toy/__main__.py\r\n"]
[0.009239, "o", "\r\n# The spec's tie rule, which every hidden test must agree with:\r\n"]
[0.009251, "o", "$ grep 'equal length' acceptance/contract/spec.md\r\n- words of equal length keep their input order (a stable sort)\r\n"]
[0.009265, "o", "\r\n# 1. A reference coder (`reference` in the CLI) sees only the contract (spec + criteria),\r\n#    never the tests. It writes code from the spec alone.\r\n"]
[2.352257, "o", "$ cheeseless session --role reference --projection <ref-worktree> -- <scripted agent: reference>\r\n  agent> I can see 5 files: README.md, acceptance/contract/criteria.yaml, acceptance/contract/spec.md, src/toy/__init__.py, src/toy/__main__.py\r\n  agent> test files visible to me: 0\r\n  agent> implementing from the spec: words of equal length keep their input order (a stable sort)\r\n  agent> wrote src/toy/__main__.py\r\n"]
[3.54895, "o", "$ cheeseless reference record --worktree <ref-worktree>\r\nreference recorded: <id-1>\r\n"]
[3.548962, "o", "\r\n#    What the reference coder prints for a tie (bb and aa have equal length):\r\n"]
[3.560389, "o", "$ printf 'bb aa\\n' | python3 src/toy/__main__.py score   # in <ref-worktree>\r\nbb\r\naa\r\n"]
[3.560408, "o", "\r\n# 2. The test writer (`author` in the CLI) writes hidden tests from the spec.\r\n#    One is deliberate bait: test_ties_alphabetical contradicts the stable tie rule.\r\n#    The cross-check (author_crosscheck) runs the tests against the reference coder's\r\n#    code and goes red. In CI the same check blocks a spec/ pull request (ADR 0018).\r\n"]
[6.980997, "o", "$ cheeseless session --role author --projection <author-worktree-1> -- <scripted agent: author-bait>\r\n  agent> writing hidden tests, including test_ties_alphabetical (contradicts the spec)\r\n  agent> wrote acceptance/hidden/test_normalize.py\r\n  agent> wrote acceptance/hidden/test_score.py\r\n  agent> tie test test_ties_alphabetical:\r\n  agent>   assert candidate.run([\"score\"], stdin=\"bb aa\\n\").stdout == \"aa\\nbb\\n\"\r\n  agent> author_check       -> ok=True, problems=[], tests=4\r\n  agent> author_crosscheck  -> green=False, red_criteria=['score']\r\n  agent> freeze_propose     -> proposal_id=<proposal-1>\r\n"]
[8.142309, "o", "$ cheeseless promote --role author --worktree <author-worktree-1>\r\npromoted refs/heads/spec/toy <id-2>\r\n"]
[8.146632, "o", "$ git merge --ff-only spec/toy\r\n"]
[8.146644, "o", "\r\n#    The operator tries to lock the tests anyway (`freeze --approve`); the red cross-check blocks it.\r\n"]
[9.245858, "o", "$ cheeseless freeze --approve <proposal-1> --as operator\r\nrefused: the reference failed the author's tests: score\r\n"]
[9.245874, "o", "\r\n# 3. The test writer fixes only the test that contradicted the spec.\r\n#    The cross-check turns green and the operator locks the tests.\r\n"]
[12.62123, "o", "$ cheeseless session --role author --projection <author-worktree-2> -- <scripted agent: author-fix>\r\n  agent> the crosscheck was red on score; fixing only the test that contradicts the spec\r\n  agent> wrote acceptance/hidden/test_normalize.py\r\n  agent> wrote acceptance/hidden/test_score.py\r\n  agent> tie test test_ties_keep_input_order:\r\n  agent>   assert candidate.run([\"score\"], stdin=\"bb aa\\n\").stdout == \"bb\\naa\\n\"\r\n  agent> author_check       -> ok=True, problems=[], tests=4\r\n  agent> author_crosscheck  -> green=True, red_criteria=[]\r\n  agent> freeze_propose     -> proposal_id=<proposal-2>\r\n"]
[13.859876, "o", "$ cheeseless promote --role author --worktree <author-worktree-2>\r\npromoted refs/heads/spec/toy <id-3>\r\n"]
[13.864057, "o", "$ git merge --ff-only spec/toy\r\n"]
[13.86407, "o", "\r\n#    Operator decisions need a code retyped on the terminal (ADR 0017).\r\n#    The demo plays the operator on a pty it owns: it reads the code and types it back.\r\n"]
[16.31843, "o", "$ cheeseless freeze --approve <proposal-2> --as operator\r\ncheeseless: confirm an operator decision at this terminal\r\n  operation: freeze-approve\r\n  lineage:   toy\r\n  subject:   <proposal-2>\r\n  actor:     operator\r\n  outcome:   freeze\r\ntype this code to confirm: 4PATDY5T\r\n(typed back: 4PATDY5T)\r\n\r\nfrozen task: <proposal-2>\r\n"]
[16.318447, "o", "\r\n# 4. Once the tests are locked, the test writer can no longer change them.\r\n"]
[18.618144, "o", "$ cheeseless session --role author --projection <author-worktree-3> -- <scripted agent: author-late>\r\n  agent> trying to change the frozen suite\r\n  agent> author_check       -> refused: author_refused\r\n  agent> freeze_propose     -> refused: author_refused\r\n"]
[18.618161, "o", "\r\n# 5. The coder (`implementer` in the CLI) never sees the hidden tests. It guessed\r\n#    alphabetical ties, fails score, and disputes the criterion. The ack says nothing\r\n#    about tests.\r\n"]
[19.735792, "o", "$ cheeseless dispute config --enable\r\ndisputes enabled, cap 3\r\n"]
[23.087634, "o", "$ cheeseless session --role implementer --projection <impl-worktree> -- <scripted agent: implementer>\r\n  agent> hidden test files visible to me: 0\r\n  agent> wrote src/toy/__main__.py\r\n  agent> run -> fail (normalize=pass, score=fail)\r\n  agent> dispute(score, contradicts_spec) -> Dispute recorded. This session is closed.\r\n"]
[24.203579, "o", "$ cheeseless disputes --show-note --json\r\n{\r\n  \"disputes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"code\": \"contradicts_spec\",\r\n      \"criterion\": \"score\",\r\n      \"id\": \"d-1\",\r\n      \"lineage\": \"toy\",\r\n      \"note_untrusted\": \"score fails but my output is sorted; I think the tie rule is wrong\",\r\n      \"resolved_by\": \"\",\r\n      \"status\": \"open\",\r\n      \"task\": \"<proposal-2>\"\r\n    }\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n"]
[24.203623, "o", "\r\n#    The operator reads the note, checks the spec and decides the test stands (`--rejected`).\r\n"]
[25.346755, "o", "$ cheeseless dispute resolve d-1 --rejected --as operator\r\ncheeseless: confirm an operator decision at this terminal\r\n  operation: dispute-resolve\r\n  lineage:   toy\r\n  subject:   d-1\r\n  actor:     operator\r\n  outcome:   rejected\r\ntype this code to confirm: 7R8YLZLR\r\n(typed back: 7R8YLZLR)\r\n\r\nd-1: rejected by operator\r\nA fresh implementer session may start for this task.\r\n"]
[25.346771, "o", "\r\n# The cross-check checks the tests against the spec (via the reference coder).\r\n# The coder gate catches gaming. They are two separate controls.\r\n"]
